WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.548
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level two.

2
00:00:05.848 --> 00:00:09.153
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.453 --> 00:00:15.611
Unit eight: Marketing & Advertising. Today you will emphasise ideas with cleft sentences.

4
00:00:15.911 --> 00:00:18.575
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.533 --> 00:00:22.441
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.283 --> 00:00:24.633
Target audience.

7
00:00:25.617 --> 00:00:29.160
Target audience means the group of people an advertisement is made for.

8
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:31.738
The target audience was teenagers.

9
00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:35.293
Your turn. Say: Target audience.

10
00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:39.425
Target audience.

11
00:00:40.183 --> 00:00:41.521
Brand awareness.

12
00:00:42.517 --> 00:00:45.886
Brand awareness means how well consumers recognise a brand.

13
00:00:46.483 --> 00:00:49.098
Sponsoring the match raised brand awareness.

14
00:00:49.683 --> 00:00:52.672
Your turn. Say: Brand awareness.

15
00:00:55.533 --> 00:00:57.068
Brand awareness.

16
00:00:57.817 --> 00:00:59.456
Advertising campaign.

17
00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:04.563
Advertising campaign means a planned series of advertisements with one goal.

18
00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:07.730
The advertising campaign ran for three months.

19
00:01:08.317 --> 00:01:11.666
Your turn. Say: Advertising campaign.

20
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:16.221
Advertising campaign.

21
00:01:16.983 --> 00:01:18.414
Consumer insight.

22
00:01:19.417 --> 00:01:23.901
Consumer insight means a deeper understanding of why customers behave as they do.

23
00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:27.155
A consumer insight inspired the slogan.

24
00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:30.704
Your turn. Say: Consumer insight.

25
00:01:33.567 --> 00:01:35.055
Consumer insight.

26
00:01:35.817 --> 00:01:37.433
Market segmentation.

27
00:01:38.417 --> 00:01:43.017
Market segmentation means dividing customers into groups with similar needs.

28
00:01:43.617 --> 00:01:46.870
Market segmentation helped the firm target students.

29
00:01:47.483 --> 00:01:50.716
Your turn. Say: Market segmentation.

30
00:01:53.567 --> 00:01:55.636
Market segmentation.

31
00:01:56.383 --> 00:01:57.559
Call to action.

32
00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:02.198
Call to action means a phrase that urges the audience to do something.

33
00:02:02.783 --> 00:02:04.922
'Buy now' is a common call to action.

34
00:02:05.517 --> 00:02:08.181
Your turn. Say: Call to action.

35
00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:12.255
Call to action.

36
00:02:13.017 --> 00:02:14.505
Return on investment.

37
00:02:15.517 --> 00:02:19.525
Return on investment means the profit gained compared with the money spent.

38
00:02:20.117 --> 00:02:22.987
The campaign delivered a strong return on investment.

39
00:02:23.583 --> 00:02:26.514
Your turn. Say: Return on investment.

40
00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:31.122
Return on investment.

41
00:02:31.883 --> 00:02:33.128
Brand loyalty.

42
00:02:34.117 --> 00:02:37.695
Brand loyalty means the habit of buying the same brand repeatedly.

43
00:02:38.283 --> 00:02:40.933
Brand loyalty keeps customers returning.

44
00:02:41.517 --> 00:02:44.262
Your turn. Say: Brand loyalty.

45
00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.380
Brand loyalty.

46
00:02:49.167 --> 00:02:52.725
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:53.583 --> 00:03:01.669
Visal, an article says 'What persuades customers is a clear call to action.' Why not simply 'A clear call to action persuades customers'?

48
00:03:02.783 --> 00:03:11.310
The cleft sentence adds emphasis. 'What' + clause + is/was + focus puts the important idea at the end.

49
00:03:12.417 --> 00:03:14.219
Are there other cleft forms?

50
00:03:15.317 --> 00:03:21.417
'It was the consumer insight that made the campaign work.' We move the key phrase after 'it was' to stress it.

51
00:03:22.517 --> 00:03:24.981
Why does marketing writing love emphasis?

52
00:03:26.083 --> 00:03:34.703
Because every campaign wants the target audience to remember one thing: the brand. Cleft sentences help it stand out.

53
00:03:35.867 --> 00:03:37.541
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:38.383 --> 00:03:41.962
Grammar focus: Cleft sentences for emphasis.

55
00:03:42.262 --> 00:03:43.472
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:44.183 --> 00:03:47.309
What persuades customers is a clear call to action.

57
00:03:48.217 --> 00:03:51.250
It was the consumer insight that made the campaign work.

58
00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:54.591
What the brand needs is stronger loyalty.

59
00:03:55.533 --> 00:04:04.769
Use What + clause + is/was + focus, or It is/was + focus + that + clause, to emphasise one idea. Do not drop 'that' in the it-cleft.

60
00:04:05.517 --> 00:04:09.005
Be careful! Don't say: It was the insight made it work.

61
00:04:10.967 --> 00:04:13.582
Say: It was the insight that made it work.

62
00:04:13.882 --> 00:04:15.521
Keep 'that' in an it-cleft.

63
00:04:16.333 --> 00:04:18.800
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:21.402
What Makes an Advert Work.

65
00:04:21.702 --> 00:04:25.385
An advertising campaign starts with a clear target audience.

66
00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:31.174
What marketers need first is a consumer insight, because it explains how people think.

67
00:04:32.167 --> 00:04:36.755
It is market segmentation that lets a brand speak to each group in its own way.

68
00:04:37.767 --> 00:04:42.146
What customers remember is usually a simple message and a strong call to action.

69
00:04:43.133 --> 00:04:47.269
In the end, it is brand loyalty that produces the best return on investment.

70
00:04:48.367 --> 00:04:52.392
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:56.503
blank persuades customers is a clear call to action.

72
00:04:56.803 --> 00:04:59.633
A, What. B, It. C, That.

73
00:05:03.167 --> 00:05:04.795
The answer is A: What.

74
00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:09.227
How well consumers recognise a brand is brand blank.

75
00:05:09.527 --> 00:05:13.784
A, awareness. B, loyalty. C, segmentation.

76
00:05:17.333 --> 00:05:19.832
The answer is A: awareness.

77
00:05:20.983 --> 00:05:24.144
Profit compared with money spent is the blank on investment.

78
00:05:24.444 --> 00:05:27.958
A, return. B, call. C, target.

79
00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:33.372
The answer is A: return.

80
00:05:34.517 --> 00:05:36.238
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:36.538 --> 00:05:42.838
A, It was the insight made it work.. B, It was the insight that made it work.. C, What the insight made it work..

82
00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:49.561
The answer is B: It was the insight that made it work..

83
00:05:50.717 --> 00:05:54.806
According to the reading, the best return on investment comes from brand…

84
00:05:55.106 --> 00:05:58.771
A, loyalty. B, colour. C, slogans.

85
00:06:02.333 --> 00:06:04.031
The answer is A: loyalty.

86
00:06:05.233 --> 00:06:08.420
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:09.283 --> 00:06:12.885
What is an advertisement that made a strong impression on you, and why?

88
00:06:21.683 --> 00:06:23.091
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:23.391 --> 00:06:43.951
One advertisement that impressed me was a short film about a family sharing a meal. What made it powerful was the story, not the product. It was the emotion that stayed in my memory, and the brand name appeared only at the end. As a result, I still remember the message and the company.

90
00:06:44.251 --> 00:06:45.902
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:46.817 --> 00:06:51.350
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and cleft sentences for emphasis.

92
00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:55.835
Today's value is creativity. Use your imagination when you play.

93
00:06:56.135 --> 00:06:58.787
See you in Unit nine. Goodbye!

94
00:06:59.087 --> 00:07:02.343
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

